// ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Rozdział jedenasty — Obława (biały wilk). Sroga zima po narodzinach
//  Marysi (Jaromir ma dwadzieścia lat). Wilki we wsi: obrona obory
//  (stary pies przeżywa) albo pilnowanie drzwi (pies ginie, zagryzając
//  wilka). Gajowy Pawlik ogłasza obławę i nagrodę za białego wilka,
//  Antek widzi w nim oczy Franka (obietnica). W młodniku: wydać wilka
//  (ranny ucieka do boru), zmylić obławę albo — z celnością z dzieciństwa —
//  rzucić kamieniem w lufę (kolba, blizna, odrabianie u dziedzica).
//  Wiosną szczenię z rodu psa.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

=== rozdzial_jedenasty ===
# tlo: mroz_izba
# rozdzial: Chapter Eleven
# tytul: The Hunt
In Marysia’s first winter, after Epiphany, the frost bit so hard that tree trunks split in the night with a crack like a gunshot, sparrows dropped from the branches frozen hard as stones, and the ice on the lake boomed until morning. Water froze in the bucket in the passage before anyone had a chance to use it.
In the cottage they kept the fire going from dawn till night. Hanka slept with Marysia right up against the stove, wrapped in two featherbeds, and every few hours Jaromir got up to throw on more wood. {noga_ojca == zlamana:His father limped worse than ever in the cold|His father no longer got up from the bench at all}, and his mother steeped bran for hot poultices on his knee.{ uklad_z_mamunami == oddane_lata: Jaromir’s bones ached too – dully, stubbornly, as if the winter had made its nest inside him.}
Marysia had begun to laugh at the sight of Jaromir; she grabbed at his fingers and put into her mouth everything within reach of her hands. In the evenings, when the frost crackled outside the window, Hanka sang to her by the cradle, and Jaromir sat beside them thinking that never in his life had he been so happy.
Only from the forest, bolder each night, came the howling. # pokaz: wycie # dalej
-> owczarnia

= owczarnia
# tlo: owczarnia_noc
In the middle of January the wolves came into the village.
First, at the Wójciks’, they found a snowdrift dug up one morning and blood on the snow. Then at Staś’s three sheep were killed in a single night – though their sheepfold stood in the very middle of Zapadlina, where no one had ever seen a wolf. People began carrying their poultry indoors and propping their gates shut with poles.
Before dawn on Sunday Jaromir was woken by the screaming of the sheep. Barefoot, he rushed to the window. In the moonlight he saw grey shadows circling the cowshed – five, perhaps six – and one white one, larger than the rest, standing motionless at the edge of the field.{ ekwipunek ? szczeniak: {imie_psa} – old by now, his muzzle gone grey – growled by the door till his flanks shook, and raked the boards with his claws.} # pokaz: wilki
# pytanie: What will Jaromir do?
*   [Run out with the axe and defend the cowshed.]
    ~ noc_wilkow = bronil_obory
    He seized his grandfather’s axe and burst out into the yard. The frost caught the breath in his throat. The wolves turned towards him, heads low to the ground, fangs glinting in their jaws.{ ekwipunek ? szczeniak: {imie_psa} leapt after him and flung himself at the nearest, though he was half its size.}
    Behind Jaromir, Hanka screamed. The door to the passage stood wide open and one of the grey ones had slipped inside, straight towards the room where Marysia slept. Before Jaromir could turn back, his wife drove the wolf over the threshold with a brand snatched from the stove – but not before its teeth found her forearm.
    The white wolf howled – short and sharp, like a command. The whole pack fell back from the cowshed as if someone had jerked it on a rope. The old dog-wolf let the last shadow slip past him and only then vanished into the darkness behind Staś’s barn.{ ekwipunek ? szczeniak: {imie_psa} came back with a torn ear and a bloodied shoulder, but alive.} Until dawn Jaromir sat in the passage binding the wounds of {ekwipunek ? szczeniak:the dog and Hanka|Hanka}. Hers was deep; the scar of the fangs stayed with her all her life. # pokaz: rozkaz # dalej
