# tlo: gajowy_karczma
Towards the end of January the gamekeeper from the manor, Pawlik, drove into Zapadlina by sleigh – a huge man, red with cold, a double-barrelled gun slung across his back. He stopped outside the inn and called the people together. # pokaz: gajowy
“His lordship the squire orders a wolf hunt,” he announced. “Saturday at dawn. One man from every cottage, with a rattle or a pitchfork. The guns from the manor will stand at the gap below the forest, and you’ll drive the wolves out of the young wood straight onto them.” He ran his eyes over the gathering and added, more quietly: “For the hide of that white one the squire pays ten silver roubles. Mr Urbaniak’s putting up as much again.”
A murmur ran through the crowd. Twenty roubles was more than many a farmer in Zapadlina had seen in his whole life.
That evening Antek came to Jaromir’s cottage. He sat down on the bench, turned his cap round and round in his hands for a long while, and could not begin. # pokaz: antek
“I’ve seen him,” he said at last. “The white one. By the old wayside shrine. Watching.” His voice broke. “He’s got Franek’s eyes. I know. It’s daft. But I’d never mistake those eyes.”
# pytanie: What will Jaromir say?
