    “The marshes!” Jaromir shouted, turning away. “He’s gone for the marshes!”
    The gamekeeper swore and ran downhill through the reeds, a few of the beaters after him.{ obietnica_antkowi: “There! I saw him!” Antek called out, and set off after them, waving his rattle so that no one could be in any doubt.} When Jaromir looked back at the hollow, there was no one beneath the trunk. Only snow still sifted from a spruce branch, knocked loose in flight. # pokaz: zmylka
    From below, down by the marshes, came a crack and a cry. Under the drifts the ice there was wafer-thin: young Kuba, the wheelwright’s lad from Bukowiec, had gone through up to his chest into the black water. They hauled him out with poles, stiff with cold, and carried him to the sleighs on sheepskin coats. # dalej
