    ~ oblawa_wilk = rzucil_kamieniem
    The gamekeeper raised the gun to his shoulder. Jaromir stooped, scrabbled a stone the size of an egg from under the snow and threw it – with the same sureness with which, as a boy, he had aimed at a sheaf on the field balk, practising for days on end to beat Hanka.
    The stone struck the barrel. The shot went into a snowdrift in a puff of powder. The white wolf leapt the trunk and vanished into the thicket. # pokaz: kamien
    The gamekeeper rounded on Jaromir, purple with rage, and without a word smashed the butt of his gun into his face. Jaromir fell flat on his back. Blood ran from his split cheek, warm and salty.
    “The squire’ll hear of this,” Pawlik panted. “You’ll pay me for that powder.” # dalej
