By evening the guns had killed five wolves. The gamekeeper had their hides nailed to the doors of the manor barn in Bukowiec for everyone to see. The white one was not among them.
{ oblawa_wilk == rzucil_kamieniem:
    For the stone the commune court in Bukowiec sentenced Jaromir to a week in the lock-up and payment for the powder. There was nothing to pay the fine with, so he worked it off for the manor, three weeks of hauling timber. The scar under his eye stayed with him for ever – narrow and pale, like the mark of a claw.
}
{ oblawa_wilk == wydal_wilka:
    In the night a howl came from the forest – not the usual kind, but long, hoarse and full of pain. Jaromir lay with his eyes open, listening to the voice draw nearer the village, fade and return. Towards morning the cows began to thrash about in the cowshed as if something were circling the walls, and when he went out with a lantern, nothing hung in the frosty air but a heavy smell of wet fur and blood. # pokaz: wycie
    Hanka did not sleep until dawn. She sat by the cradle with a Candlemas candle in her hands, and when Jaromir reached to take it from her, she pushed his hand away.
“Not you,” she said quietly. “Not today.” # dalej
    -> odwilz
}
The next morning, when Jaromir went out to chop firewood, a hare lay on the block by the fence – fresh, still warm, its neck bitten through with a single clean snap. As he bent over it, one short bark came from the young wood – soft, almost a dog’s – and then nothing more. # pokaz: zajac
When he told her, Hanka was silent for a long time. Then she took the hare and began to skin it.
{obietnica_antkowi:“Fool,” she whispered, to no one in particular. “Good, foolish Franek.”|“Fool,” she whispered, to no one in particular. “Good, foolish…”} # dalej
